<title>BRAZIL: Brazil Nov petroleum use down from Oct - Petrobras.</title>
<headline>Brazil Nov petroleum use down from Oct - Petrobras.</headline>
<dateline>RIO DE JANEIRO 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Consumption in Brazil of petroleum products averaged 1,578,600 barrels per day (bpd) in November, down 7.6 percent from October, state-controlled oil ompany Petrobras said in a statement.</p>
<p>The figure represents a 2.7 percent increase on the same month last year, it added.</p>
<p>Of the total, diesel accounted for 554,900 barrels bpd and gasoline 291,900 bpd, it said.</p>
<p>-- Caroline Bulloch, Rio de Janeiro newsroom, 5521 5074151</p>
</text>
